1
00:00:06,521 --> 00:00:10,860
-- FORTRESS FILMS --

2
00:00:15,679 --> 00:00:18,530
HELIX TECHNOLOGIES PRESENTS...

3
00:00:18,884 --> 00:00:22,219
THE RESPAWN MACHINE

4
00:00:26,634 --> 00:00:28,568
"It's eternity in there!"

5
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:35,473
"My eyes hurt."

6
00:00:55,481 --> 00:00:57,628
-- EMESIS BLUE --

7
00:01:02,358 --> 00:01:04,465
Thursday

8
00:01:04,465 --> 00:01:06,950
October 31, 1968

9
00:01:06,950 --> 00:01:09,446
7:57pm

10
00:02:42,798 --> 00:02:45,000
...Hey... Doc...?

11
00:03:00,001 --> 00:03:01,961
I know it's late, but...

12
00:03:01,961 --> 00:03:03,809
Mind if I ask you something?

13
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,856
You ever have bad dreams?

14
00:03:12,683 --> 00:03:14,503
--JULES ARCHIBALD KIDNAPPED--

15
00:03:15,298 --> 00:03:16,566
So tell me about it.

16
00:03:17,355 --> 00:03:18,924
Well, I was in the bathroom, right...

17
00:03:18,924 --> 00:03:22,696
...and as I was brushing my teeth, all my teeth started to fall out.

18
00:03:23,443 --> 00:03:25,678
There was blood all over the basin...

19
00:03:25,678 --> 00:03:26,827
...it was horrible.

20
00:03:27,395 --> 00:03:29,026
Are you worried about something?

21
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:30,701
Yeah, actually.

22
00:03:31,390 --> 00:03:33,426
You ever get the feeling like you're being watched?

23
00:03:34,675 --> 00:03:35,924
What do you mean?

24
00:03:36,424 --> 00:03:37,491
When I went to bed last night...

25
00:03:37,991 --> 00:03:41,184
...I could swear there was someone standing outside my window.

26
00:03:41,833 --> 00:03:43,120
Oh, don't be ridiculous.

27
00:03:43,292 --> 00:03:44,708
Someone was just passing by.

28
00:03:45,042 --> 00:03:46,888
Doc... I was on the second floor.

29
00:03:48,442 --> 00:03:50,063
Have you spoken to your mother about this?

30
00:03:50,347 --> 00:03:51,698
She says it's all in my head.

31
00:03:53,722 --> 00:03:55,746
Well, there's nothing wrong with your teeth.

32
00:03:56,246 --> 00:03:56,746
Here.

33
00:03:57,246 --> 00:03:59,448
Take one of these tonight. They should help.

34
00:03:59,709 --> 00:04:01,485
Come on Doc, I don't need this stuff.

35
00:04:01,985 --> 00:04:04,682
I think you do, Scout. This doesn't seem normal.

36
00:04:05,182 --> 00:04:06,462
You sound like my mother.

37
00:04:07,857 --> 00:04:08,755
Help me out here.

38
00:04:09,338 --> 00:04:11,126
She must be thrilled you're moving back in with her.

39
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:13,289
After being laid off? Are you kidding me?

40
00:04:13,908 --> 00:04:16,441
I'm gonna sue the hell out of BLU for what they did to me.

41
00:04:16,808 --> 00:04:18,310
Well... you wouldn't be the first.

42
00:04:18,810 --> 00:04:19,310
Doc?

43
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:21,068
If they ever hit you with something...

44
00:04:21,622 --> 00:04:23,452
...you hit back twice as hard. You hear me?

45
00:04:23,952 --> 00:04:25,019
Well, it's getting late.

46
00:04:25,307 --> 00:04:26,728
Come on, I'll give you a ride.

47
00:04:29,245 --> 00:04:31,762
Jeez. You got a whole video store in there.

48
00:04:34,616 --> 00:04:36,477
What the hell could've done that?

49
00:04:41,213 --> 00:04:42,618
"M" -- (1931)

50
00:04:43,348 --> 00:04:44,575
Forget about it.

51
00:04:44,625 --> 00:04:46,330
Come on, before it gets dark.

52
00:04:48,511 --> 00:04:49,629
Scout?

53
00:05:10,608 --> 00:05:16,376
-- CHAPTER ONE: GRAVEYARD SHIFT --

54
00:05:26,444 --> 00:05:30,000
"Re-elect JULES ARCHIBALD for Governor of New Mexico"

55
00:06:03,454 --> 00:06:05,078
He's here, I need my...

56
00:06:05,078 --> 00:06:06,712
...what the hell are you doing?!

57
00:06:08,463 --> 00:06:10,214
Give me that before you hurt yourself.

58
00:06:10,639 --> 00:06:12,344
You told me to keep a lookout.

59
00:06:12,844 --> 00:06:14,433
I told you to wait in the car.

60
00:06:14,433 --> 00:06:16,350
Look... what if it's an ambush?

61
00:06:16,350 --> 00:06:18,409
He's alone. This shouldn't take long.

62
00:06:18,909 --> 00:06:20,827
That ruski's twice your size.

63
00:06:21,327 --> 00:06:23,102
I just need to make him talk.

64
00:06:23,102 --> 00:06:24,311
What if he doesn't?

65
00:06:24,807 --> 00:06:26,385
Just keep an eye out for the police.

66
00:06:49,237 --> 00:06:50,897
Builders League.

67
00:06:51,397 --> 00:06:54,094
You look lost, comrade... and that suit doesn't fit you.

68
00:06:54,854 --> 00:06:57,032
I did not ask for your opinion.

69
00:06:57,032 --> 00:06:59,374
So tell me the facts. Who's the hand-off?

70
00:06:59,374 --> 00:07:00,795
Who's your new employer?

71
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:02,500
I don't know what you're talking about.

72
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,989
Who kidnapped Archibald? Was it you?

73
00:07:05,627 --> 00:07:07,627
You know the price of betrayal, friend.

74
00:07:08,052 --> 00:07:09,970
They'll throw you up against the wall for this.

75
00:07:10,892 --> 00:07:12,138
What's in the briefcase?

76
00:07:12,492 --> 00:07:14,410
It does not concern you.

77
00:07:15,716 --> 00:07:17,022
Hand it over.

78
00:07:17,522 --> 00:07:19,439
You want my briefcase?

79
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,921
--This is 189. Reporting a 503 at a local cemetary.--

80
00:07:32,921 --> 00:07:35,165
--The vehicle in question is a black hearse.--

81
00:07:36,019 --> 00:07:38,858
--10-9, say again... a black hearse?--

82
00:07:39,565 --> 00:07:41,123
--10-4, that is correct.--

83
00:07:41,623 --> 00:07:43,115
--189, is this a joke?--

84
00:07:43,682 --> 00:07:45,355
--Who steals a freaking hearse at this hour?--

85
00:07:46,666 --> 00:07:48,473
--You think that's funny, 189?--

86
00:07:48,973 --> 00:07:49,969
--That wasn't me.--
Oh crap.

87
00:07:49,969 --> 00:07:51,249
--Who the hell is that?--

88
00:08:27,093 --> 00:08:28,492
Hey, Stalingrad.

89
00:08:29,795 --> 00:08:30,602
Eat this!

90
00:08:36,887 --> 00:08:37,643
You're welcome.

91
00:08:38,143 --> 00:08:39,068
You idiot!

92
00:08:39,581 --> 00:08:41,795
He was our only lead and now he's dead!

93
00:08:42,474 --> 00:08:44,145
Oh... so you were just talking?

94
00:08:47,264 --> 00:08:48,352
We have to get out of here.

95
00:08:48,852 --> 00:08:49,990
What about the body?

96
00:08:50,563 --> 00:08:51,916
I left my camera in the car.

97
00:08:52,416 --> 00:08:53,058
Fetch it for me.

98
00:08:53,593 --> 00:08:54,128
Now.

99
00:09:01,396 --> 00:09:04,341
Don't think I'm gonna save your skinny ass again, prick.

100
00:09:33,930 --> 00:09:35,381
What the hell happened?

101
00:09:35,750 --> 00:09:37,029
He took the briefcase!

102
00:09:42,273 --> 00:09:48,237
--CHAPTER TWO: "DINNER'S READY!"--

103
00:09:52,103 --> 00:09:53,701
Hey, doc.

104
00:09:53,792 --> 00:09:54,870
Yes?

105
00:09:55,370 --> 00:09:58,086
What did you mean when you said I'm not the first?

106
00:09:58,441 --> 00:10:00,000
You talkin' about the accident?

107
00:10:02,233 --> 00:10:03,686
There have been others.

108
00:10:04,254 --> 00:10:06,523
You tellin' me that this has happened before?

109
00:10:08,077 --> 00:10:08,993
Doc...

110
00:10:09,667 --> 00:10:11,550
What is wrong with the Respawn Machine?

111
00:10:12,125 --> 00:10:14,330
It doesn't always work like it's supposed to.

112
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,438
Some get stuck inside trying to come through.

113
00:10:18,072 --> 00:10:20,194
What the hell are you talking about, Doc?

114
00:10:20,694 --> 00:10:23,462
I've only seen it happen once... on the frontlines.

115
00:10:23,962 --> 00:10:26,376
He came through screaming... horribly.

116
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:29,219
When I ran into see what happened, I... I...

117
00:10:29,719 --> 00:10:31,282
What did you see, Doc?

118
00:10:31,782 --> 00:10:33,699
You don't want to know.

119
00:10:42,383 --> 00:10:43,766
Thanks for the ride, Doc.

120
00:10:44,333 --> 00:10:46,747
You sure you don't wanna come in? At least say "hi" to Ma?

121
00:10:47,247 --> 00:10:49,590
Tell her I did, Scout. I have to get back to the office.

122
00:10:50,125 --> 00:10:52,255
You really gotta get out more often, Doc.

123
00:10:54,806 --> 00:10:56,082
Catch you later, alright?

124
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:57,546
I'll see you soon.

125
00:11:05,149 --> 00:11:07,295
Hey Ma! I'm home.

126
00:11:07,934 --> 00:11:09,919
Where the hell have you been? You're soaked!

127
00:11:10,278 --> 00:11:12,337
Just getting a check-up, Ma. I'm fine.

128
00:11:22,217 --> 00:11:26,498
--♫...Soon the Man in Black will come...♫--

129
00:11:26,498 --> 00:11:28,313
So how was the doctor, dear?

130
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:29,575
Fine?

131
00:11:29,575 --> 00:11:30,937
Did you ask him to stop by?

132
00:11:30,937 --> 00:11:33,280
Tried. I feel bad for the guy.

133
00:11:33,634 --> 00:11:35,959
What's the matter with him?
--♫...he'll make mincemeat out of you!♫--

134
00:11:35,959 --> 00:11:36,884
--You're out.-- 

135
00:11:36,884 --> 00:11:38,234
I think he's on something.

136
00:11:38,234 --> 00:11:40,789
--♫Just you wait, it won't be long...♫--

137
00:11:53,871 --> 00:11:56,109
--That's a nice ball.--

138
00:11:56,747 --> 00:11:57,972
Dinner's ready, dear!

139
00:11:58,259 --> 00:11:58,901
Okay, hang on.

140
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:00,560
Hello?

141
00:12:01,498 --> 00:12:02,507
--'Thanks for the ride, doc.'--

142
00:12:02,916 --> 00:12:05,593
--'You sure you don't wanna come in? At least say "hi" to Ma?'--

143
00:12:06,093 --> 00:12:06,593
What did you...?

144
00:12:07,479 --> 00:12:08,365
Who is this?

145
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:10,770
--'You really gotta get out more often, Doc.'--

146
00:12:11,129 --> 00:12:11,629
What--

147
00:12:11,629 --> 00:12:13,688
What the hell is this?! Who are you?!

148
00:12:14,042 --> 00:12:16,031
--'Hey Ma! I'm home.'--

149
00:12:59,619 --> 00:13:00,418
Hello?

150
00:13:54,214 --> 00:13:57,106
So the hand-off was an undertaker?

151
00:13:57,250 --> 00:13:58,388
Almost.

152
00:13:58,888 --> 00:14:00,354
What could be in that briefcase?

153
00:14:00,862 --> 00:14:03,922
Money... gold... diamonds?

154
00:14:03,922 --> 00:14:06,053
I don't think this is about money.

155
00:14:06,553 --> 00:14:07,195
Is it a bomb?

156
00:14:07,549 --> 00:14:10,231
If it was, he wouldn't hit me over the head with one.

157
00:14:10,231 --> 00:14:11,865
What if it's Archibald's severed head?

158
00:14:11,865 --> 00:14:13,428
Enough, Soldier!

159
00:14:13,428 --> 00:14:15,709
If we don't find out where he is, they'll have all our heads.

160
00:14:17,143 --> 00:14:18,364
What the hell do you think you're doing?

161
00:14:18,364 --> 00:14:19,797
I think I know who to ask.

162
00:14:20,859 --> 00:14:22,701
Soldier, that only receives. It doesn't transmit.

163
00:14:22,701 --> 00:14:23,201
Breaker-breaker!

164
00:14:23,201 --> 00:14:26,890
This is 185. Gonna need an update on that stolen hearse.

165
00:14:27,174 --> 00:14:29,504
--Roger 185. This is 187.--

166
00:14:29,504 --> 00:14:31,884
--I have visual on a black hearse heading south on Brixton.--

167
00:14:31,884 --> 00:14:33,530
10-4. Tail it!

168
00:14:34,292 --> 00:14:36,329
--He's pulling up on Purgatory Avenue. I'm gonna intercept.--

169
00:14:38,205 --> 00:14:39,230
Soldier...

170
00:14:40,024 --> 00:14:41,811
--Sir, I'm gonna need you to roll down your window.--

171
00:14:41,811 --> 00:14:43,244
--I can't see your face.--

172
00:14:50,736 --> 00:14:51,920
What street was that?

173
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:52,420
Purgatory.

174
00:15:34,946 --> 00:15:36,590
Can't see anything.

175
00:15:36,590 --> 00:15:39,075
Forget it. We got an all-units call downtown.

176
00:15:39,967 --> 00:15:41,459
Some night, huh?

177
00:16:53,622 --> 00:16:54,652
Hello?

178
00:16:55,152 --> 00:16:56,219
--Hey, Doc?--

179
00:16:56,219 --> 00:16:58,420
Oh thank God, Scout! Are you alright?

180
00:16:59,271 --> 00:17:02,887
--I know it's late but... mind if I ask you something?--

181
00:17:02,887 --> 00:17:05,868
What? Scout, where are you?

182
00:17:06,293 --> 00:17:08,578
--'You ever get the feeling like you're being watched?'--

183
00:17:15,611 --> 00:17:17,073
What the hell have you done with him?!

184
00:17:26,287 --> 00:17:29,433
--CONAGHER SLAUGHTERHOUSE--

185
00:17:32,917 --> 00:17:37,420
--CHAPTER THREE: INTEL HELL--

186
00:17:40,637 --> 00:17:43,074
I've been working downtown for over thirty years, now...

187
00:17:43,074 --> 00:17:45,346
...I ain't ever seen nothin' this bad.

188
00:17:45,346 --> 00:17:46,767
Pelizzari got tagged.

189
00:17:46,767 --> 00:17:49,252
Don't worry about it. We'll get you patched up in no time.

190
00:17:49,252 --> 00:17:51,736
Nobody comes in here except paramedics, you hear me?

191
00:17:52,646 --> 00:17:55,186
And somebody get these clowns off my crime scene.

192
00:17:55,186 --> 00:17:57,603
I don't need this right now!
- For the last time, we are federal agents. 

193
00:17:57,603 --> 00:18:00,000
I am Detective Mannix. This is Lieutenant Columbo.

194
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,130
We are looking for a very dangerous criminal.

195
00:18:02,630 --> 00:18:05,327
Will somebody run a background check on these bozos?

196
00:18:05,327 --> 00:18:07,315
There ain't no way they're FBI.

197
00:18:07,315 --> 00:18:08,194
--TERMINATION NOTICE--

198
00:18:08,194 --> 00:18:10,137
Is this him? I want to talk to him.

199
00:18:10,137 --> 00:18:11,842
No - you ain't talkin' to him!

200
00:18:13,181 --> 00:18:15,371
You. Tell me exactly what happened.

201
00:18:15,871 --> 00:18:18,249
He had to be on drugs or something, I...

202
00:18:18,249 --> 00:18:21,331
...tried to bring him down, but... he just kept coming at me...
--SIGNED, BLUTARCH MANN, CEO OF BLU INDUSTRIES--

203
00:18:21,331 --> 00:18:23,331
...it was like a nightmare.

204
00:18:23,331 --> 00:18:26,674
Yeah, the poor bastard got his own sidearm in the gut.

205
00:18:27,170 --> 00:18:30,009
Chief. They just found 187's body stuffed inside a dumpster.

206
00:18:30,435 --> 00:18:31,362
Jesus Christ!

207
00:18:33,417 --> 00:18:35,658
Agh! I'm dying over here!

208
00:18:35,658 --> 00:18:37,717
How did he escape? What was he driving?

209
00:18:37,717 --> 00:18:39,717
Look, I think you've asked enough questions here, pal.

210
00:18:40,355 --> 00:18:41,274
...Ambulance!

211
00:18:41,274 --> 00:18:43,759
See look, he needs a doctor, so why don't you just...

212
00:18:43,759 --> 00:18:45,000
No, he was... driving a...

213
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,201
...Goddamn ambulance!

214
00:18:47,839 --> 00:18:52,030
Alright, everyone step outside. There's too many people in here for Christ sake.

215
00:18:52,339 --> 00:18:53,499
Soldier!

216
00:18:55,909 --> 00:18:57,707
Get in the car.

217
00:19:21,025 --> 00:19:22,661
--CONAGHER SLAUGHTERHOUSE--

218
00:20:14,646 --> 00:20:15,839
Check the bathroom.

219
00:20:22,997 --> 00:20:24,522
Storm's cut the power.

220
00:20:25,808 --> 00:20:28,582
The mirror's shattered... there's blood all over the sink.

221
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:31,343
Christ.

222
00:20:32,335 --> 00:20:34,178
Must've been a fight or some...

223
00:20:36,423 --> 00:20:38,030
My God...

224
00:20:38,030 --> 00:20:40,089
It's his latest victim!

225
00:20:41,009 --> 00:20:42,638
It's a model, you idiot.

226
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:47,668
This is worse than I thought.

227
00:20:48,168 --> 00:20:50,582
You know, they made me take a bunch of this stuff.

228
00:20:51,252 --> 00:20:52,489
Said I was seeing things.

229
00:20:52,989 --> 00:20:54,552
And did the medication work?

230
00:20:55,075 --> 00:20:57,228
I don't know. I never took any of it.

231
00:20:57,228 --> 00:20:58,012
Right.

232
00:21:03,457 --> 00:21:04,372
No - don't!

233
00:21:05,427 --> 00:21:06,269
Hello?

234
00:21:06,269 --> 00:21:08,754
--Hello? Who is this?--

235
00:21:08,754 --> 00:21:11,030
Who am I? Who the hell are you?

236
00:21:11,030 --> 00:21:11,955
Who is this?

237
00:21:11,955 --> 00:21:12,455
--What?--

238
00:21:12,455 --> 00:21:13,309
It's him!

239
00:21:13,831 --> 00:21:15,000
Listen to me, punk.

240
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:20,603
You're not gonna think this is funny when I strangle you to death with your own stethoscope.

241
00:21:20,603 --> 00:21:21,316
--Who is this?--

242
00:21:21,316 --> 00:21:24,510
It's the voice of God, you son-of-a-bitch - and I'm coming for you!

243
00:22:04,626 --> 00:22:07,020
--RESUPPLY--

244
00:24:59,911 --> 00:25:00,691
Wait, Scout!

245
00:25:00,691 --> 00:25:02,396
I'm trying to help you!

246
00:25:03,601 --> 00:25:06,444
If I had a gun, I'd shoot you - you sick bastard!

247
00:25:07,648 --> 00:25:08,923
No! Stop!

248
00:25:47,323 --> 00:25:49,222
You look lost, boy.

249
00:25:52,461 --> 00:25:53,574
Now brother...

250
00:25:54,074 --> 00:25:57,197
...I do believe that you were the one who chained up that coffin.

251
00:25:57,771 --> 00:26:01,109
Indeed I did, brother. Up to specification.

252
00:26:01,747 --> 00:26:03,165
So how'd he get out?

253
00:26:05,611 --> 00:26:06,569
Dumbass.

254
00:26:07,452 --> 00:26:08,689
Well, go on then.

255
00:26:10,091 --> 00:26:11,139
Say somethin'.

256
00:26:18,265 --> 00:26:20,571
Well, whoever let you out...

257
00:26:21,350 --> 00:26:23,385
...I'm glad they did, because...

258
00:26:23,598 --> 00:26:24,098
...I like company.

259
00:26:32,605 --> 00:26:34,520
Why does he get to have all the fun?

260
00:27:16,405 --> 00:27:17,693
Check the ambulance.

261
00:27:25,761 --> 00:27:26,529
Nothing.

262
00:27:27,096 --> 00:27:28,159
We need to call for backup.

263
00:27:28,826 --> 00:27:30,000
I got it right here.

264
00:27:35,032 --> 00:27:37,619
You've had that thing in my car this whole time?

265
00:27:38,187 --> 00:27:38,755
For emergencies.

266
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:41,561
And just what do you plan to do with it?

267
00:27:44,254 --> 00:27:46,674
I'm gonna use it to jump across this ravine.

268
00:27:46,674 --> 00:27:48,733
You really have lost your mind haven't you?

269
00:27:48,733 --> 00:27:50,591
What? I've done it before!

270
00:27:50,591 --> 00:27:52,579
Put that down before you get us killed!

271
00:27:58,621 --> 00:27:59,575
Get down!

272
00:28:54,150 --> 00:28:56,118
Hey Dell! You haven't called me in a while!

273
00:28:56,118 --> 00:28:58,177
How's Dustbowl workin' out, brother?

274
00:28:58,177 --> 00:29:00,000
--Dustbowl is gone.--

275
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:00,925
Gone?!

276
00:29:00,925 --> 00:29:02,630
--You heard me. There's nothing left of it.--

277
00:29:02,630 --> 00:29:03,343
How?!

278
00:29:03,343 --> 00:29:05,997
--We're still trying to figure that out. It doesn't look good.--

279
00:29:05,997 --> 00:29:08,281
What about my little brother? Is he alright?

280
00:29:08,281 --> 00:29:11,262
--Listen, I'm coming to the Slaughterhouse now. Is the briefcase secure?--

281
00:29:12,191 --> 00:29:13,333
Sure.

282
00:29:13,758 --> 00:29:15,888
I swear to God, if anything happens to my brother, I'm gonna-

283
00:29:15,888 --> 00:29:17,026
--Shut up and listen to me...--

284
00:29:17,026 --> 00:29:19,369
--(UNINTELLIGABLE)--

285
00:29:19,369 --> 00:29:21,580
You're so goddamn inconsiderate.

286
00:29:22,229 --> 00:29:23,020
SHUT UP!

287
00:29:23,868 --> 00:29:24,716
--Did he get out?--

288
00:29:25,216 --> 00:29:26,708
Yeah, who knows how.

289
00:29:29,309 --> 00:29:30,492
Look, when are you gonna be back?

290
00:29:30,492 --> 00:29:31,925
We shouldn't have to deal with this.

291
00:29:32,425 --> 00:29:33,917
--Don't let the briefcase out of your sight!--

292
00:29:34,465 --> 00:29:36,076
And what about my brother...

293
00:32:58,801 --> 00:33:00,522
What the hell's goin' on in there?

294
00:33:03,095 --> 00:33:04,888
I asked you a question, dumbass.

295
00:33:05,388 --> 00:33:06,739
I said what the hell are you...

296
00:33:08,458 --> 00:33:10,177
Now that ain't a toy, son...

297
00:33:10,673 --> 00:33:11,870
Put it down.

298
00:33:13,075 --> 00:33:13,575
Now.

299
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:17,385
Now don't do nothin' stupid, boy...

300
00:33:18,016 --> 00:33:20,561
You got no idea who you're dealin' with...

301
00:33:40,832 --> 00:33:42,041
I woulda got you...

302
00:34:31,984 --> 00:34:38,196
--CHAPTER FOUR: CROSSROADS--

303
00:34:47,977 --> 00:34:51,268
I am never going to find Archibald in this excrement.

304
00:34:51,764 --> 00:34:55,859
Back in the war, we would spend weeks stuck in wet dugouts like this...

305
00:34:55,859 --> 00:34:57,918
...with water up to your ankles!

306
00:34:57,918 --> 00:35:02,033
They were built only six feet wide, but they could go on for miles!

307
00:35:02,533 --> 00:35:04,096
Kill me now!

308
00:35:09,458 --> 00:35:12,056
You have no comprehension of what you're getting into!

309
00:35:12,056 --> 00:35:13,903
I have a pretty damn good idea.

310
00:35:14,665 --> 00:35:16,348
We should have called for backup.

311
00:35:16,348 --> 00:35:18,124
And what the hell do you think I'm doing?

312
00:35:18,124 --> 00:35:20,124
I just saved you from a bullet to the head!

313
00:35:20,124 --> 00:35:21,758
And who was it that told them we were coming?

314
00:35:22,869 --> 00:35:25,468
Who's been killing our leads and getting the police involved?

315
00:35:25,827 --> 00:35:28,240
You have compromised this entire operation!

316
00:35:28,240 --> 00:35:30,240
What about all those pictures?

317
00:35:30,240 --> 00:35:32,087
That's evidence we can use, right?

318
00:35:32,087 --> 00:35:34,359
They were in the car - you idiot!

319
00:35:34,359 --> 00:35:35,710
Now I have nothing!

320
00:35:35,710 --> 00:35:36,919
Because of you!

321
00:35:36,919 --> 00:35:39,758
You stupid bastard - you amateur!

322
00:35:41,031 --> 00:35:44,572
I hope you can swim because you're going right back out the way you came!

323
00:35:45,427 --> 00:35:46,707
You gonna shoot me?

324
00:35:46,707 --> 00:35:48,069
We're done.

325
00:35:48,069 --> 00:35:50,849
I don't care what wretched batallion you think you come from.

326
00:35:50,849 --> 00:35:52,920
You are NOT coming with me.

327
00:35:52,920 --> 00:35:54,767
You shot one of your own before?

328
00:35:54,767 --> 00:35:56,685
Get out of my way.

329
00:35:56,685 --> 00:35:58,331
Archibald teach you that?

330
00:36:05,561 --> 00:36:06,249
Jesus!

331
00:36:17,944 --> 00:36:21,244
You better drop that rifle before I come over there and put my foot up your...

332
00:36:22,264 --> 00:36:23,709
Who the hell is out there?

333
00:36:23,709 --> 00:36:26,560
Looks like Ray Charles traded the piano for an M40.

334
00:36:27,126 --> 00:36:27,692
What?

335
00:36:27,692 --> 00:36:28,546
I've got an idea.

336
00:36:37,346 --> 00:36:38,802
What are you - blind?

337
00:36:39,302 --> 00:36:41,716
Come on! Right here! Take your best shot!

338
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:02,338
You think I didn't come prepared?

339
00:37:02,338 --> 00:37:04,338
How did you know he wouldn't shoot you in the head?

340
00:37:04,838 --> 00:37:05,338
I didn't.

341
00:37:16,394 --> 00:37:19,128
Let's finish him off right here and now.

342
00:37:21,679 --> 00:37:23,378
Let him bleed.

343
00:38:29,434 --> 00:38:31,348
You drop it.

344
00:38:33,509 --> 00:38:34,961
Take off the mask.

345
00:38:44,646 --> 00:38:45,961
SOLDIER!

346
00:38:45,961 --> 00:38:47,536
DON'T LEAVE ME!

347
00:41:28,496 --> 00:41:30,000
Soldier!

348
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:32,130
What are you doing? There's nothing for you here!

349
00:42:28,406 --> 00:42:29,432
Oi!

350
00:42:32,799 --> 00:42:34,040
You gonna finish that?

351
00:42:55,090 --> 00:42:57,116
I'm looking for Jules Archibald.

352
00:42:57,616 --> 00:42:58,612
Who's askin'?

353
00:42:58,612 --> 00:43:00,000
His rescue.

354
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:01,952
'Fraid you're gonna be disappointed!

355
00:43:01,952 --> 00:43:04,082
I wanna know what the hell is going on here.

356
00:43:04,082 --> 00:43:07,842
I don't know! Man's probably mincemeat by now!

357
00:43:07,842 --> 00:43:11,248
I've already lost one man. I'm not gonna lose another.

358
00:43:11,248 --> 00:43:12,952
Then you're a dead man!

359
00:43:12,952 --> 00:43:17,220
You haven't lost both eyes yet, Cyclops, so tell me what you've seen.

360
00:43:17,220 --> 00:43:18,641
Conagher brothers.

361
00:43:18,641 --> 00:43:21,622
They run the joint, but this is RED territory.

362
00:43:21,622 --> 00:43:23,397
Not anymore.

363
00:43:23,397 --> 00:43:25,528
Who's the guy you were just talkin' to?

364
00:43:25,528 --> 00:43:26,879
What guy?

365
00:43:31,345 --> 00:43:33,047
I don't have time for this.

366
00:43:33,047 --> 00:43:34,551
Wait!

367
00:43:35,067 --> 00:43:36,858
You gotta get me outta here.

368
00:43:36,858 --> 00:43:38,138
Why the hell should I?

369
00:43:38,685 --> 00:43:41,925
There's a whole stash of guns locked in a keep upstairs.

370
00:43:42,563 --> 00:43:44,291
I can getchya in.

371
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:36,646
--It's longer than you think...--

372
00:45:37,497 --> 00:45:39,551
--...I seen the other side...---

373
00:45:40,231 --> 00:45:41,549
--...It's longer than you think...--

374
00:46:42,645 --> 00:46:43,508
Come on!

375
00:46:46,560 --> 00:46:47,627
--GOODBYE--

376
00:48:10,015 --> 00:48:11,124
Stop it!

377
00:48:13,079 --> 00:48:14,396
Don't you get it?

378
00:48:15,965 --> 00:48:17,250
We're trapped.

379
00:48:20,692 --> 00:48:22,646
He's trying to kill us.

380
00:49:47,273 --> 00:49:49,889
--Patient appears to have died from a bullet to the heart.--

381
00:49:50,417 --> 00:49:53,922
--Normally we have papers signed before doing these things but...--

382
00:49:55,165 --> 00:49:56,408
--...ah, no matter.--

383
00:49:57,337 --> 00:49:59,400
--To hell with Helix, the old fools.--

384
00:50:01,172 --> 00:50:02,482
--They don't deserve this...--

385
00:50:08,011 --> 00:50:08,992
--My God!--

386
00:50:10,709 --> 00:50:11,433
--NO!--

387
00:50:25,112 --> 00:50:27,394
BUILDERS LEAGUE...

388
00:51:08,006 --> 00:51:09,490
What's wrong?

389
00:51:11,900 --> 00:51:12,768
HELLO?!

390
00:51:13,382 --> 00:51:14,563
SOMEONE HELP ME!

391
00:51:45,354 --> 00:51:46,645
SHOOT IT! SHOOT IT!

392
00:52:15,496 --> 00:52:16,193
Hey!

393
00:52:33,558 --> 00:52:34,435
Go!

394
00:54:00,692 --> 00:54:05,426
--CHAPTER FIVE: THE DOORWAY--

395
00:54:10,189 --> 00:54:12,095
Corporal, come over here.

396
00:54:14,782 --> 00:54:16,831
You want a promotion - here it is.

397
00:54:18,106 --> 00:54:19,381
What's the charge?

398
00:54:20,345 --> 00:54:21,735
Treason.

399
00:54:31,287 --> 00:54:32,901
What's it going to take Corporal?

400
00:54:36,107 --> 00:54:37,470
I want a new car.

401
00:54:38,901 --> 00:54:40,757
Done. Anything else?

402
00:54:43,639 --> 00:54:46,167
My own personal assistant.

403
00:54:46,830 --> 00:54:48,697
Anything you like, Corporal.

404
00:54:54,620 --> 00:54:57,070
How about a vacation, old boy?

405
00:54:58,197 --> 00:55:00,316
I think I've earned it.

406
00:55:18,318 --> 00:55:20,180
You think you can get away with this?

407
00:55:22,024 --> 00:55:24,719
Builders League will destroy you for what you've done!

408
00:55:28,059 --> 00:55:30,000
Don't you get it, you mute freak?!

409
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:32,272
I'm a protected man!

410
00:55:34,967 --> 00:55:36,386
What do you want?

411
00:56:17,210 --> 00:56:18,286
I don't believe it.

412
00:56:19,073 --> 00:56:20,497
On your feet, Cyclops.

413
00:56:20,997 --> 00:56:22,773
I think I lost my piece.

414
00:56:23,553 --> 00:56:25,278
Can't go back for it now.

415
00:56:28,833 --> 00:56:30,899
You don't work for the Conaghers, do you?

416
00:56:32,070 --> 00:56:33,666
I killed the Conaghers.

417
00:56:36,076 --> 00:56:37,276
Who gave you that order?

418
00:56:38,062 --> 00:56:40,833
They tried to kill me. Is that enough?

419
00:56:44,079 --> 00:56:45,711
That doesn't belong to you.

420
00:56:46,211 --> 00:56:47,845
I can explain.

421
00:56:48,345 --> 00:56:50,334
I can't see a bloody thing!

422
00:56:51,045 --> 00:56:51,756
Don't move.

423
00:57:01,568 --> 00:57:05,143
He's gotta be a sleeper agent. I know their type.

424
00:57:05,643 --> 00:57:07,702
I saw the devil in them eyes, man...

425
00:57:14,425 --> 00:57:15,992
How far down are we?

426
00:57:23,150 --> 00:57:24,038
You hear that?

427
00:57:30,819 --> 00:57:32,284
Mr. Archibald?

428
00:57:37,174 --> 00:57:39,519
Oh, thank God! A rescue!

429
00:57:39,519 --> 00:57:42,582
You have to get me out of here before I contract something!

430
00:57:42,582 --> 00:57:43,649
Are you injured, sir?

431
00:57:43,649 --> 00:57:45,436
I'm about to have a heart attack.

432
00:57:45,436 --> 00:57:49,066
Now, are you going to stand there or can you unlock this bloody door?

433
00:57:49,857 --> 00:57:52,845
You're right where you belong you fat, crooked bastard!

434
00:57:52,845 --> 00:57:54,904
Smart bloody leper, aren't you?

435
00:57:55,404 --> 00:57:55,904
Soldier...

436
00:57:55,904 --> 00:57:58,034
Why are you dragging this corpse around?

437
00:57:58,034 --> 00:58:00,000
What the hell this man call me?

438
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:00,948
He's been handy, sir.

439
00:58:00,948 --> 00:58:02,582
He's got none left!

440
00:58:02,582 --> 00:58:04,653
Are you conspiring with the enemy, Soldier?

441
00:58:04,653 --> 00:58:06,145
I'm just trying to help, sir.

442
00:58:06,145 --> 00:58:07,720
Then stop wasting my time!

443
00:58:48,474 --> 00:58:52,226
You want me to do it, don't you? But I won't you can't make me...

444
00:58:52,781 --> 00:58:54,045
You can't make me!

445
00:59:13,110 --> 00:59:14,536
Mr. Archibald?

446
00:59:15,404 --> 00:59:16,272
Cyclops?

447
00:59:47,457 --> 00:59:48,901
Hello, Dell.

448
00:59:49,401 --> 00:59:51,035
Long night, eh?

449
00:59:52,545 --> 00:59:54,055
Longer than you think.

450
00:59:56,159 --> 00:59:57,554
Care for a drink?

451
00:59:58,972 --> 01:00:00,000
Love one.

452
01:00:03,740 --> 01:00:06,347
I thought you were miles away, lad.

453
01:00:07,269 --> 01:00:08,687
Where you been hiding?

454
01:00:10,556 --> 01:00:11,788
Who says I've been hidin'?

455
01:00:14,432 --> 01:00:16,226
Your brothers thought you were dead.

456
01:00:22,109 --> 01:00:24,382
Relapse is a hell of a thing, ain't it?

457
01:00:25,594 --> 01:00:26,593
Too right.

458
01:00:40,060 --> 01:00:41,889
"Longer than you think..."

459
01:00:42,967 --> 01:00:44,045
It is.

460
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:45,855
What?

461
01:00:48,245 --> 01:00:50,635
When they figured out how to bring us back...

462
01:00:50,635 --> 01:00:54,183
...some of us would tell stories 'bout what we saw on the other side.

463
01:00:55,104 --> 01:00:57,088
We saw old friends... family...

464
01:00:57,938 --> 01:00:59,300
...mostly strangers.

465
01:00:59,896 --> 01:01:01,555
I spoke to my grandfather.

466
01:01:03,581 --> 01:01:05,253
He's been dead for thirty years.

467
01:01:08,017 --> 01:01:09,558
What'd he tell ya?

468
01:01:12,251 --> 01:01:13,885
"It's eternity in there."

469
01:01:44,432 --> 01:01:45,946
--TERMINAL--

470
01:02:24,147 --> 01:02:26,361
--HELIX TECHNOLOGIES--

471
01:02:29,504 --> 01:02:31,230
-- >RUNNING STARTUP PROGRAM... -

472
01:02:31,230 --> 01:02:33,289
-- >LOCALIZING DATA... --

473
01:02:33,289 --> 01:02:35,289
-- >SEARCHING... --

474
01:02:35,714 --> 01:02:36,763
-- > [1] FILE FOUND... -

475
01:02:36,763 --> 01:02:38,964
-- >WARNING! FILE CORRUPTION DETECTED... --

476
01:02:39,464 --> 01:02:42,374
-- >PROCEED? [YES/NO] --

477
01:02:44,641 --> 01:02:46,766
-- >PROCEED? [YES/NO] --

478
01:02:54,459 --> 01:02:55,206
--Blutarch?--

479
01:02:55,206 --> 01:02:56,769
--Blutarch - can you hear me?--

480
01:02:58,047 --> 01:03:01,168
--Lower your voice, Blutarch! I can hear you just fine.--

481
01:03:01,168 --> 01:03:02,672
--Am I coming through clear?--

482
01:03:04,109 --> 01:03:06,184
--No, Blutarch - this is a telephone call.--

483
01:03:06,751 --> 01:03:08,397
--Much faster than air mail.--

484
01:03:08,942 --> 01:03:09,487
--Blutarch, we...--

485
01:03:10,248 --> 01:03:12,497
--What do you mean "who is this"? It's Jules Archibald.--

486
01:03:13,018 --> 01:03:15,000
--We last spoke in Dallas, after you-know-what.--

487
01:03:15,638 --> 01:03:16,291
--Remember?--

488
01:03:17,217 --> 01:03:19,631
--Yes, I'm calling about the project we discussed.--

489
01:03:20,833 --> 01:03:23,381
--No! Not the pregnancy machine - the other one!--

490
01:03:23,806 --> 01:03:25,936
--Yes, there's been a slight hiccup, so-to-speak.--

491
01:03:25,936 --> 01:03:30,000
--The Respawn Machine works - it technically works, Blutarch. However...--

492
01:03:30,575 --> 01:03:32,639
--No. You see, that's the problem.--

493
01:03:32,993 --> 01:03:35,773
--They say we lost about ninety percent of the test subjects.--

494
01:03:35,773 --> 01:03:36,355
--WHAT?!--

495
01:03:36,993 --> 01:03:39,727
--I... I know you're upset, Blutarch, but the good news is...--

496
01:03:39,727 --> 01:03:42,719
--...we've found about ten of them that are Respawn Compatible.--

497
01:03:43,640 --> 01:03:45,000
--Er, hold on a moment...--

498
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:46,847
--What the hell is going on?--

499
01:03:47,414 --> 01:03:49,757
--He shot himself? Oh, bloody hell.--

500
01:03:49,757 --> 01:03:52,480
--Just throw him in the pit with the others.--

501
01:03:52,834 --> 01:03:54,893
--Excuse me - nine, Blutarch.--

502
01:03:54,893 --> 01:03:56,881
--You promised me an army, Archibald.--

503
01:03:56,881 --> 01:03:59,153
--Well, think of the money you'll save!--

504
01:03:59,153 --> 01:04:01,141
--Mercenaries are very cheap these days!--

505
01:04:01,141 --> 01:04:05,185
--With a Respawn Machine on every frontline, there will be no worry!--

506
01:04:05,185 --> 01:04:08,024
--You'll surely win this war by the end of the financial year!--

507
01:04:08,024 --> 01:04:10,225
--We must not allow a Respawn Gap!--

508
01:04:10,225 --> 01:04:12,639
--A Respawn Gap?! You must be joking!--

509
01:04:12,639 --> 01:04:15,850
--Blutarch, I really must be going, now. Listen...--

510
01:04:15,850 --> 01:04:19,192
--...would you be interested in a new heart... liver... spleen?

511
01:04:19,192 --> 01:04:23,378
--We have about eight hundred thousand corpses on site, and we're not really sure what to do with them.--

512
01:04:23,378 --> 01:04:24,728
--Oh, I'll take one of each!--

513
01:04:24,728 --> 01:04:27,508
--I see. I'll put it on the bill.--

514
01:04:27,508 --> 01:04:28,725
--Ta-ta, Blutarch.--

515
01:04:30,676 --> 01:04:32,792
--Redmond? Jules Archibald.--

516
01:04:32,792 --> 01:04:34,780
--I have a proposition for you...--

517
01:04:40,839 --> 01:04:41,653
Please.

518
01:04:45,567 --> 01:04:47,428
-- >INITIATING MANUAL RESPAWN... --

519
01:05:03,941 --> 01:05:05,287
-- >RESTARTING METABOLIC FUNCTIONS... -

520
01:05:06,024 --> 01:05:07,611
-- >RESPAWNING... --

521
01:05:07,950 --> 01:05:09,494
--WARNING! FATAL ERROR!--

522
01:05:09,876 --> 01:05:13,731
--ENTITY UNKNOWN!--

523
01:05:14,085 --> 01:05:16,328
--RESPAWN--

524
01:06:28,551 --> 01:06:30,678
--He's here. Got him cornered.--

525
01:06:32,159 --> 01:06:33,498
--Cryo Lab.--

526
01:06:34,065 --> 01:06:34,565
--He won't get far.--

527
01:11:18,396 --> 01:11:19,811
--"Do No Harm"--

528
01:15:14,694 --> 01:15:17,564
Goldman? I'm in a fix and you have to get me out of it.

529
01:15:17,989 --> 01:15:19,989
I cannot go to trial. I simply won't.

530
01:15:20,761 --> 01:15:22,667
I'm already on thin ice with the Old Mann, and...

531
01:15:22,667 --> 01:15:27,219
...if any word gets out about that godforsaken asylum, I'll be sued into oblivion!

532
01:15:27,219 --> 01:15:28,499
Maybe even hung!

533
01:15:28,499 --> 01:15:31,054
My chances for re-election will be ruined!

534
01:15:31,054 --> 01:15:33,468
I am not going down for a war crime!

535
01:15:33,468 --> 01:15:35,315
--I told you not to make that deal.--

536
01:15:35,665 --> 01:15:38,773
So what if I made a deal with the Old Mann's brother?

537
01:15:38,773 --> 01:15:43,880
The war is their business, and mine is to drag it out for as long as humanly possible!

538
01:15:43,880 --> 01:15:47,995
That infernal - unholy - contraption is my lifeline, Goldman!

539
01:15:49,413 --> 01:15:50,437
--It might be your only way out.--

540
01:15:51,456 --> 01:15:55,027
Oh, I've thought about it, surely... as a last resort, but...

541
01:15:55,594 --> 01:15:59,067
...if I can use it to disappear for a while, it's a chance I'll have to take.

542
01:16:03,553 --> 01:16:05,204
Where am I calling from?

543
01:16:05,204 --> 01:16:07,830
That's a stupid question - you know bloody hell where I am!

544
01:16:07,830 --> 01:16:09,818
--Jules, I heard you'd been kidnapped - what's going on?--

545
01:16:09,818 --> 01:16:11,098
"Kidnapped"?

546
01:16:11,098 --> 01:16:12,803
I don't know anything about that!

547
01:16:12,803 --> 01:16:14,579
Listen very carefully, Goldman.

548
01:16:14,579 --> 01:16:16,993
I think there are people trying to kill me.

549
01:16:16,993 --> 01:16:18,993
And worse yet... I think this valium is actually-

550
01:16:18,993 --> 01:16:22,257
--To continue this call, please deposit five cents.--

551
01:16:22,257 --> 01:16:23,608
Oh, blast!

552
01:16:52,808 --> 01:16:54,438
Who the hell are you?

553
01:16:55,431 --> 01:16:57,133
It's me, Jules.

554
01:16:58,409 --> 01:17:02,144
Oh, thank God, Corporal! You've come to save me!

555
01:17:02,664 --> 01:17:04,460
Have I?

556
01:17:04,460 --> 01:17:06,460
I've always been the one to save you, Archie.

557
01:17:07,098 --> 01:17:09,795
I did your dirty work, hid it from everyone...

558
01:17:09,795 --> 01:17:11,217
...and look what it did to me!

559
01:17:11,217 --> 01:17:12,650
My God!

560
01:17:13,638 --> 01:17:16,185
Who was there to save me, Jules?

561
01:17:16,685 --> 01:17:18,957
You've never cared about anyone but yourself.

562
01:17:18,957 --> 01:17:22,505
Corporal... no! Please! For God sake!

563
01:17:23,072 --> 01:17:26,620
Well, there's no one here to protect you now.

564
01:17:26,620 --> 01:17:30,309
But... I... I've given you everything you wanted!

565
01:17:30,309 --> 01:17:33,078
And I'm giving you exactly what you deserve.

566
01:18:01,773 --> 01:18:03,521
--THE JULES ARCHIBALD FOUNDATION--

567
01:18:04,588 --> 01:18:06,435
--I'm on? Alright, fine.--

568
01:18:07,431 --> 01:18:08,427
--Hello again!--

569
01:18:08,427 --> 01:18:12,471
--If you're watching this, then I can say with complete certainty that you have survived...--

570
01:18:12,471 --> 01:18:15,000
--...Respawn Compatibility.--

571
01:18:15,000 --> 01:18:16,563
--Congratulations!--

572
01:18:16,563 --> 01:18:18,481
--If you're confused, allow me to explain.--

573
01:18:18,977 --> 01:18:21,603
--Before you were lawfully executed by the state, you signed a contract...--

574
01:18:21,603 --> 01:18:26,355
--...you signed a contract, effectively donating your mortal remains to a medical trial.--

575
01:18:26,780 --> 01:18:29,220
--The good news is you're not on death row anymore...--

576
01:18:29,220 --> 01:18:31,634
--...since you're technically already dead.--

577
01:18:31,634 --> 01:18:35,394
--Which also means you are now company property - but fear not!--

578
01:18:35,890 --> 01:18:39,225
--As promised, you all have a new job waiting for you when you get out.--

579
01:18:39,650 --> 01:18:42,985
--You are now ten of the strongest mercenaries money can buy...--

580
01:18:42,985 --> 01:18:45,567
--...and your sacrifice will reward you in time.--

581
01:18:45,992 --> 01:18:48,119
--I'll see you all on the other side.--

582
01:18:48,536 --> 01:18:51,150
--Oh, hell!--

583
01:19:32,584 --> 01:19:35,249
You really wanna die for that fat bastard?

584
01:19:41,060 --> 01:19:44,043
Don't you wanna die for something worth dying for?

585
01:19:48,933 --> 01:19:51,390
Do you have any idea how long I've waited for this?

586
01:19:52,453 --> 01:19:54,863
Longer than you think.

587
01:20:02,599 --> 01:20:04,027
What took you so long?

588
01:20:31,102 --> 01:20:32,689
See you on the other side.

589
01:20:40,769 --> 01:20:42,270
Why did you come here?

590
01:20:43,549 --> 01:20:45,425
I was trying to save somebody.

591
01:20:48,073 --> 01:20:49,303
So was I.

592
01:20:55,257 --> 01:20:56,436
We shouldn't be here.

593
01:21:07,705 --> 01:21:10,642
--EMESIS PHARMACEUTICALS--

594
01:21:31,480 --> 01:21:36,979
--CHAPTER SIX: KATABASIS --

595
01:21:42,467 --> 01:21:43,560
Hello, doctor.

596
01:21:52,136 --> 01:21:53,151
Open it.

597
01:21:53,943 --> 01:21:54,735
I can't!

598
01:21:55,235 --> 01:21:56,444
I insist.

599
01:21:57,195 --> 01:21:58,441
It's not mine.

600
01:21:58,441 --> 01:21:59,933
LIAR!

601
01:21:59,933 --> 01:22:01,579
Tell him how you got the case, Fritz.

602
01:22:02,004 --> 01:22:02,992
I stole it.

603
01:22:04,197 --> 01:22:05,794
Impossible.

604
01:22:05,794 --> 01:22:06,866
Forget this!

605
01:22:06,866 --> 01:22:07,508
Where is Archibald?

606
01:22:07,508 --> 01:22:09,780
Archibald is dead!

607
01:22:10,559 --> 01:22:13,035
Everything this man has told you is a lie.

608
01:22:13,035 --> 01:22:15,744
He killed him... and the boy.

609
01:22:16,098 --> 01:22:17,662
No... that's not true!

610
01:22:17,662 --> 01:22:19,296
What is true to you?

611
01:22:19,934 --> 01:22:22,393
Or you? Who ran away?

612
01:22:25,653 --> 01:22:28,439
I am the only sane man here.

613
01:22:28,439 --> 01:22:30,073
I took a bullet for you.

614
01:22:30,782 --> 01:22:34,685
I should have shot you myself.

615
01:22:40,072 --> 01:22:41,217
You first.

616
01:23:12,106 --> 01:23:14,289
You're gonna make it, Fritz.

617
01:23:14,649 --> 01:23:16,001
I know.

618
01:23:17,419 --> 01:23:17,919
NO!

619
01:23:21,799 --> 01:23:24,120
Goodbye, Dr. Ludwig.

620
01:23:26,847 --> 01:23:29,574
Now you know how it feels.

621
01:23:32,404 --> 01:23:35,234
You won. Go.

622
01:23:39,109 --> 01:23:40,362
And Soldier?

623
01:23:41,933 --> 01:23:44,142
I'll see you at the funeral.

624
01:26:30,417 --> 01:26:33,438
Our true enemy has yet to reveal himself.

625
01:32:46,704 --> 01:32:48,886
Mr. Doe, my name is Agent Stemmons.

626
01:32:49,516 --> 01:32:52,839
You don't know me, but I know all about you.

627
01:32:53,980 --> 01:32:55,688
I'm here to debrief you on the situation.

628
01:32:57,161 --> 01:32:58,918
Conagher Slaughterhouse is a dead zone.

629
01:32:59,831 --> 01:33:00,744
There's nothing left of it.

630
01:33:01,511 --> 01:33:02,774
And I think that's for the best.

631
01:33:03,789 --> 01:33:06,151
It was actually scheduled for demolition months ago...

632
01:33:06,694 --> 01:33:08,868
...but Governor Archibald prevented that from happening.

633
01:33:09,891 --> 01:33:11,694
He had his secrets, Mr. Doe.

634
01:33:12,362 --> 01:33:14,164
But you discovered something that we find...

635
01:33:14,701 --> 01:33:16,372
...deeply disturbing.

636
01:33:17,483 --> 01:33:18,310
Something that...

637
01:33:18,815 --> 01:33:20,879
...threatens the foundation of this company.

638
01:33:21,843 --> 01:33:25,146
Whatever it was you saw inside Conagher Slaughterhouse...

639
01:33:25,689 --> 01:33:27,295
...you are not to speak of it with anyone.

640
01:33:28,382 --> 01:33:29,115
Not a soul.

641
01:33:30,509 --> 01:33:31,903
Do I make myself clear?

642
01:33:34,395 --> 01:33:35,044
Good.

643
01:33:36,085 --> 01:33:37,764
Is there anything else you want to tell me?

644
01:33:47,274 --> 01:33:49,271
Governor Archibald's funeral is on Sunday.

645
01:33:50,831 --> 01:33:51,540
Wear black.

646
01:33:58,942 --> 01:34:00,000
Cheer up, Mr. Doe.

647
01:34:01,068 --> 01:34:02,136
I think your friend will pull through.

648
01:34:17,959 --> 01:34:23,929
--CHAPTER SEVEN: BLOOD BROTHERS--

649
01:34:30,985 --> 01:34:32,655
Glad you could make it, Detective.

650
01:34:33,151 --> 01:34:35,281
I'm sorry for your loss. I heard you two were very close.

651
01:34:41,234 --> 01:34:42,956
--FOLLOW THE SCRIPT--

652
01:34:45,509 --> 01:34:48,062
Ah, here he is. The Mann of the hour.

653
01:34:48,843 --> 01:34:50,191
You know who I am.

654
01:34:50,759 --> 01:34:52,036
Blutarch Mann.

655
01:34:52,744 --> 01:34:54,641
Nice to finally meet you.

656
01:34:55,141 --> 01:34:56,350
You knew my friend Jules?

657
01:34:58,477 --> 01:35:00,000
Better than anyone.

658
01:35:00,992 --> 01:35:04,312
Fifty-eight years old. He was just a kid.

659
01:35:04,599 --> 01:35:08,430
I met him in 1960. Right after the election.

660
01:35:08,784 --> 01:35:10,631
He was going on and on:

661
01:35:10,631 --> 01:35:12,903
"How do we get rid of this son-of-a-bitch?"

662
01:35:13,474 --> 01:35:15,000
Shall we find you a seat, Mr. Mann?

663
01:35:15,000 --> 01:35:18,052
Oh yes - yes! I need to sit down!

664
01:35:25,069 --> 01:35:27,471
Funerals are an absolute waste of money.

665
01:35:28,818 --> 01:35:29,672
Like war?

666
01:35:30,984 --> 01:35:34,989
If I couldn't strike my brother down, I thought God would eventually do it for me.

667
01:35:35,556 --> 01:35:39,175
But I'm not closer to beating Redmond than I was a hundred years ago!

668
01:35:39,600 --> 01:35:40,951
Speak of the devil...

669
01:35:41,801 --> 01:35:43,293
...and he shall appear.

670
01:35:43,293 --> 01:35:45,919
I thought I smelled something dead in here!

671
01:35:45,919 --> 01:35:48,970
I've just come to offer my condolences, Blutarch.

672
01:35:48,970 --> 01:35:53,084
Balderdash! What was MY friend doing in YOUR compound, Redmond?

673
01:35:53,084 --> 01:35:55,072
I don't know what you're talking about!

674
01:35:55,497 --> 01:35:57,344
He was like the brother I never had!

675
01:35:57,653 --> 01:35:59,575
You slaughtered him! Admit it!

676
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:00,996
Gentlemen.

677
01:36:06,039 --> 01:36:07,396
Thank you all for coming.

678
01:36:09,657 --> 01:36:12,981
We are here to honor the memory of Jules Archibald.

679
01:36:13,406 --> 01:36:18,159
And his loss, I'm sure, has come as a shock to all of us.

680
01:36:19,082 --> 01:36:22,131
Jules carried Builders League for as long as I can remember.

681
01:36:23,253 --> 01:36:27,919
And though he's gone, we won't forget the sacrifices he made for this company.

682
01:36:28,911 --> 01:36:32,693
Of course, with the accolades out of the way, I'm sure you all want to know what happened.

683
01:36:33,487 --> 01:36:38,534
As you know, Jules was recently abducted from his home by some kind of underground cult.

684
01:36:38,959 --> 01:36:41,018
The rescue operation had gone awry.

685
01:36:41,518 --> 01:36:43,932
And while myself and my colleague managed to escape...

686
01:36:45,354 --> 01:36:46,140
Jules...

687
01:36:47,326 --> 01:36:48,110
...died.

688
01:36:49,180 --> 01:36:51,313
Perhaps my colleague could explain what happened.

689
01:37:25,475 --> 01:37:26,653
I apologize!

690
01:37:27,377 --> 01:37:29,377
Jules Archibald was murdered.

691
01:37:35,604 --> 01:37:37,011
By this man!

692
01:37:37,518 --> 01:37:40,931
Formerly Dr. Fritz Ludwig. One of our own men.

693
01:37:41,405 --> 01:37:45,150
A schizophrenic psychopath and an addict of his own medicine.

694
01:37:46,224 --> 01:37:48,716
He also had an addiction for his own patients.

695
01:37:49,917 --> 01:37:52,536
This boy has been missing since Halloween night.

696
01:37:53,032 --> 01:37:56,013
His mother was found beheaded with a hacksaw!

697
01:37:56,013 --> 01:37:58,001
Is this really necessary?

698
01:37:58,514 --> 01:38:03,209
I am simply illustrating a point that this man was capable of kidnap and murder!

699
01:38:04,137 --> 01:38:06,199
How did we let this happen?

700
01:38:06,816 --> 01:38:11,119
Archibald is dead... because we failed him.

701
01:38:11,615 --> 01:38:12,680
Did you kill him?

702
01:38:14,168 --> 01:38:15,865
I beg your pardon?

703
01:38:18,984 --> 01:38:20,640
Did you kill the bastard or not?

704
01:38:22,267 --> 01:38:23,469
No.

705
01:38:23,969 --> 01:38:26,028
The coward took his own life.

706
01:38:26,661 --> 01:38:28,499
Unspeakable crimes!

707
01:38:30,000 --> 01:38:33,912
This unbridled act of cruelty against our own company will not go unpunished!

708
01:38:34,337 --> 01:38:39,277
So, in Archibald's death, and in accordance to his will...

709
01:38:39,277 --> 01:38:42,226
...I will be taking his place as Chairman of the Board...

710
01:38:42,580 --> 01:38:45,000
...to end this treason and corruption...

711
01:38:45,000 --> 01:38:45,855
...once and for all!

712
01:39:03,574 --> 01:39:04,698
Get me out of here!

713
01:40:03,584 --> 01:40:04,706
STOP HIM!

714
01:40:05,301 --> 01:40:06,393
DON'T LET HIM GET AWAY!

715
01:40:10,646 --> 01:40:11,902
Can't you go any faster?!

716
01:40:12,402 --> 01:40:13,540
I'm flooring it, sir!

717
01:40:13,540 --> 01:40:15,847
They're shooting at us! Run all the red lights!

718
01:40:15,847 --> 01:40:17,765
What are they good for anyway?

719
01:40:17,765 --> 01:40:19,328
LOOK OUT!

720
01:40:25,352 --> 01:40:27,024
Help me...

721
01:41:15,857 --> 01:41:17,745
Don't kill me, man!

722
01:41:23,061 --> 01:41:24,425
You! Put your hands up!

723
01:41:27,331 --> 01:41:27,908
Johnny!

724
01:41:30,000 --> 01:41:30,670
Chief!

725
01:41:42,719 --> 01:41:44,069
Good gravel...

726
01:41:44,636 --> 01:41:45,705
...I won!

727
01:41:46,568 --> 01:41:48,210
I outlived you brother!

728
01:41:48,210 --> 01:41:50,340
I am the last Mann standing!

729
01:42:15,638 --> 01:42:17,721
--MANN BROTHERS ASSASSINATED--

730
01:43:03,436 --> 01:43:05,894
--DELL'S--

731
01:43:17,339 --> 01:43:19,288
You look lost, stranger.

732
01:43:20,918 --> 01:43:22,024
I am.

733
01:43:23,919 --> 01:43:25,247
Where you headed?

734
01:43:27,480 --> 01:43:28,933
I don't know.

735
01:43:30,000 --> 01:43:31,281
Nearest town's back the other way.

736
01:43:31,706 --> 01:43:32,926
That's not where I'm going.

737
01:43:33,939 --> 01:43:35,165
So where are you going?

738
01:43:38,121 --> 01:43:39,447
Do you have a phone?

739
01:43:40,329 --> 01:43:41,211
Nope.

740
01:43:42,400 --> 01:43:43,943
I think I'm going to be sick.

741
01:43:45,639 --> 01:43:46,981
Restroom's in the back.

742
01:44:51,231 --> 01:44:52,506
Gott helfe mir.

743
01:46:23,298 --> 01:46:24,278
Hey, Doc.

